<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palau is an island country in the western Pacific, at the western end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caroline-islands">Caroline Islands</a>, made up of about 340 islands. Ruled in turn by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1899 and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1914, whose South Seas Government sat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koror">Koror</a>, it saw hard fighting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peleliu">Peleliu</a> in 1944 and then became part of the US Trust Territory. It became independent in 1994 in free association with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palau.jpg" alt="Palau" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: John Blau Skebong Vector: Nightstallion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Palau.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
